WEBVTT

00:02.300 --> 00:05.930
<b>Hi, I'm Koge-Donbo,
the original character concept designer.</b>

00:06.030 --> 00:10.660
<b>I'm Hitomi Koshiki. I was involved with
the planning of Di Gi Charat at Broccoli.</b>

00:11.440 --> 00:16.810
<b>I'm Satsuki Yamashita, public relations
staff at Broccoli International USA.</b>

00:16.910 --> 00:19.470
<b>Today we're here</b>

00:19.580 --> 00:25.040
<b>to provide commentary
on the Di Gi Charat Original Series</b>

00:25.150 --> 00:28.590
<b>in celebration of the DVD release.</b>

00:30.990 --> 00:34.430
<b>Yes, this is an old series,</b>

00:35.460 --> 00:40.990
<b>so Koge-Donbo and I would like to reflect
on the past and talk about the series.</b>

00:41.100 --> 00:43.160
<b>So let's begin.</b>

00:43.270 --> 00:46.070
<b>This brings back memories.
How many years has it been?</b>

00:46.070 --> 00:47.470
<b>This brings back memories.
How many years has it been?</b>

00:50.110 --> 00:51.170
<b>About 5 years?</b>

00:51.280 --> 00:53.140
<b>Has it been 5 years?</b>

00:53.580 --> 00:55.310
<b>5 years?</b>

00:55.420 --> 00:59.290
<b>Oh, it's been about 4 years.</b>

01:00.790 --> 01:05.520
<b>When we first saw the storyboard
for the series, it was a shock.</b>

01:06.430 --> 01:11.160
<b>We didn't think the anime would be
like this, so we were surprised.</b>

01:13.100 --> 01:16.400
<b>Can you tell us</b>

01:16.770 --> 01:22.680
<b>how the Di Gi Charat
anime series started?</b>

01:23.110 --> 01:25.940
<b>First, we had</b>

01:27.150 --> 01:29.450
<b>a TV commercial.</b>

01:29.550 --> 01:35.050
<b>Broccoli commissioned that commercial
to an animation studio,</b>

01:35.160 --> 01:36.990
<b>and we had it made.</b>

01:37.090 --> 01:41.190
<b>The commercial was popular
among the fans,</b>

01:41.300 --> 01:49.900
<b>Note: TBS is the TV station that aired
Di Gi Charat The Original Series.</b>

01:41.300 --> 01:46.300
<b>and a producer from TBS
came to Broccoli saying that</b>

01:46.300 --> 01:49.900
<b>they would like to
create an anime series for it.</b>

01:50.010 --> 01:51.530
<b>I was very surprised.</b>

01:51.640 --> 01:55.410
<b>It was just a commercial,
and to make that into a TV show?</b>

01:55.510 --> 02:11.080
<b>Note: The four-panel manga ''Gema Gema''
is serialized in the free magazine
''From Gamers,'' published monthly.</b>

01:55.510 --> 01:59.480
<b>Aside from that, we only had
a four-panel comic strip.</b>

01:59.480 --> 02:01.150
<b>So I was excited
and worried about</b>

02:01.150 --> 02:03.990
<b>how the staff would put something
together with just that.</b>

02:03.990 --> 02:05.590
<b>We thought,</b>

02:05.590 --> 02:11.080
<b>'Is there enough material
to make an anime with this?''</b>

02:12.230 --> 02:13.320
<b>That's true.</b>

02:13.430 --> 02:16.690
<b>Di Gi Charat is known in the U.S.</b>

02:16.800 --> 02:22.290
<b>for not being the usual
30-minute anime series.</b>

02:22.970 --> 02:26.840
<b>It's an anime short that
got people intrigued.</b>

02:26.940 --> 02:32.440
<b>When it was determined that
the director was going to be Sakurai-san,</b>

02:32.550 --> 02:35.850
<b>and when we were introduced
to each other,</b>

02:35.950 --> 02:41.790
<b>he told us that he wanted to keep
the feeling of a four-panel manga.</b>

02:41.890 --> 02:48.520
<b>And the actual slot on TV
was going to be five minutes long.</b>

02:48.800 --> 02:52.390
<b>So that's how they were able
to create a show</b>

02:52.870 --> 02:56.360
<b>that retained the feeling
of the original four-panel manga.</b>

02:57.510 --> 03:01.200
<b>Because the slot was so short,</b>

03:10.590 --> 03:14.610
<b>they were able to utilize every second
and keep a good pace.</b>

03:22.700 --> 03:29.900
<b>The characters are often SD-ified
in the manga too, aren't they?</b>

03:30.010 --> 03:37.300
<b>Note: dame - no good.
''Dame art'' refers to sketch-like art.</b>

03:30.010 --> 03:34.010
<b>This is what we would call
''dame art.''</b>

03:34.740 --> 03:37.300
<b>''Dame art,'' right?</b>

03:37.410 --> 03:41.780
<b>And there's the fact that the panels
of the four-panel manga are so small</b>

03:41.880 --> 03:45.940
<b>that you can't draw
full bodies properly.</b>

03:46.450 --> 03:48.580
<b>Gamers always gets destroyed
or blown up.</b>

03:48.690 --> 03:49.850
<b>It sure does.</b>

03:49.960 --> 03:52.390
<b>We've been asked</b>

03:52.490 --> 03:59.090
<b>if it's okay to destroy our own store
in our own anime series.</b>

04:00.930 --> 04:04.490
<b>But if the fans enjoy it,
then we'd gladly destroy it.</b>

04:04.770 --> 04:08.170
<b>That's how our president Kidani feels.</b>

04:16.520 --> 04:19.780
<b>So this is the end.</b>

04:20.390 --> 04:23.910
<b>How was it?</b>

04:24.190 --> 04:29.720
<b>I don't know how many times
I said, ''I dunno.''</b>

04:29.830 --> 04:33.920
<b>But I think the unknowns are
what make this anime enjoyable.</b>

04:34.030 --> 04:35.660
<b>That's true.</b>

04:36.440 --> 04:41.740
<b>Hopefully the commentary
was helpful to viewers.</b>

04:42.070 --> 04:45.840
<b>If the fans thought
they'd understand Di Gi Charat more</b>

04:45.940 --> 04:47.810
<b>after watching the commentary,</b>

04:47.910 --> 04:51.250
<b>maybe we didn't meet
their expectations.</b>

04:51.350 --> 04:53.480
<b>Well, now they know that</b>

04:53.590 --> 04:57.890
<b>even the people who created it
don't understand it either.</b>

05:03.000 --> 05:05.120
<b>Thank you to everyone</b>

05:06.300 --> 05:12.000
<b>who bought the Di Gi Charat
Original Series DVD.</b>

05:13.470 --> 05:17.600
<b>Please feel free to comment,</b>

05:17.710 --> 05:23.550
<b>''I don't get it,''
as you watch the anime.</b>

05:23.820 --> 05:29.720
<b>I think that's the best part
of Di Gi Charat, so please enjoy it.</b>

05:43.970 --> 05:47.500
<b>Please buy the rest
of the Di Gi Charat DVDs.</b>

05:49.480 --> 05:55.070
<b>This is the original Di Gi Charat,
so please watch it and enjoy the rest.</b>

05:55.180 --> 05:57.510
<b>Please buy the manga too.
Of course.</b>

05:57.880 --> 05:59.110
<b>Products too.</b>

05:59.220 --> 06:00.210
<b>Of course.</b>

06:00.320 --> 06:02.250
<b>Please support Di Gi Charat
in the future.</b>

06:02.350 --> 06:04.650
<b>Thank you.
Thank you.</b>
